WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:10.910
If you're anything like me you like the idea
of reading but when it actually comes time

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.940
to buckle down sit on a chair pick up a book
and read you have a hard time focusing let

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.240
alone really enjoying it.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.109
And maybe you've thought to yourself "Well,
I guess I'm just not a reader.

00:00:20.109 --> 00:00:22.900
I'm more of an action-based learner, you know,
I learn by doing."

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.429
But deep down you know that by not reading
books you're missing out on some of the important,

00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:30.099
in depth and profound insights ever recorded.

00:00:30.099 --> 00:00:34.690
So how can people like us, people who aren't
naturally bookworms, actually read books,

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:37.200
retain their information, and actually learn
to enjoy it?

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.829
Well in this video I'm going over 5 powerful
strategies that will help you not only read

00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:46.820
more, but find that you enjoy reading more
than you ever possibly thought you ever could.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.469
Tip number one: If you want to start reading,
don't overachieve.

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:53.100
It's very easy to say "yeah I'm gonna read
a book a week from now on."

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.620
But your past is telling.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:55.620
You're not going to.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.510
So in order to break into the habit of reading,
you need to set your standards almost comically

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:00.510
low.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:01.510
I'm talking one page a day.

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:05.909
Reading one page only takes about 60 seconds
if you're an average-speed reader, and, well,

00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:07.780
it's an extremely easy task.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.720
But remember: It's just as easy not to do,
so make sure you do it.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.060
Don't make not doing it an option.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:16.580
And if you want to keep reading after you've
read your daily page - go for it, but the

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:26.000
important thing is to get that one page in.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.970
Tip number two is: read before going on the
internet.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:33.579
You don't need me to tell you that the internet
is an ADHD inducing place full of cheap dopamine

00:01:33.579 --> 00:01:35.150
highs and shallow thinking.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:39.460
Checking your Facebook, Instagram, Pinterest
and Reddit before reading a good book is like

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.409
binge eating Skittles before tasting a fine
wine.

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:46.060
The wine will taste way worse and you'll feel
too sick to drink it anyways.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:49.259
Point being - read books before your brain
is zapped by the internet.

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:52.750
A great way to do this, obviously, is to read
first thing in the morning.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.399
Which brings me right to my next tip.

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:56.719
Tip number three is bunch your habits.

00:01:56.719 --> 00:02:01.250
Habit bunching is when you pair an already
existing habit that you enjoy doing with a

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:02.579
habit that you're trying to work on.

00:02:02.579 --> 00:02:06.060
If it's a habit for you to drink a nice hot
cup of coffee in the morning, then pair that

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.070
habit with reading.

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:10.769
An easy way to do this is to put the book
you want to read next to your coffee maker

00:02:10.769 --> 00:02:13.810
in the morning so when you get up and make
yourself a cup of coffee you'll see the book

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:14.989
and you'll grab it and go.

00:02:14.989 --> 00:02:18.680
By bunching an already existing habit with
one you're trying to work on, not only will

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.800
it be easier to work on that new habit but
the enjoyability of the first habit may even

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.150
rub off on the second one.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.410
Tip number four is: Try audiobooks.

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:30.400
Listening to audiobooks is a great way to
soak in the information of a book while still

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.510
being able to multitask.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.519
One of my favorite things to do, especially
if I have to read a book for school, is to

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:37.230
listen to the book while I'm working out.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:40.690
If you enjoy working out like I do this counts
as habit bunching.

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:41.690
My camera just overheated.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:45.450
Where was I. Audible is personal favorite
place to get audiobooks and while the subscription

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:46.450
isn't free.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:47.450
Oh yeah!

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:51.360
So if you find yourself at about a book-a-month
pace then audible's free book system pays

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.360
for itself.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.560
I think that math checks out.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.989
My fifth and final tip is: Change your attitude.

00:02:55.989 --> 00:03:01.060
And this tip, while it may seem not very practical
or hands on, it's probably the most important.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:04.989
Because if you self-identify as someone who
hates reading, you're building up unnecessary

00:03:04.989 --> 00:03:08.040
mental resistance towards something you're
trying to do more of.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.040
That's dumb.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.519
So if you start identifying as someone who
enjoys reading, you'll break down mental barriers,

00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:16.269
and you'll find the previous four tips a lot
easier to do.

00:03:16.269 --> 00:03:17.269
So there you go.

00:03:17.269 --> 00:03:19.970
Hopefully you find these tips as useful as
I currently do.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.709
I used to be someone who didn't like reading...

00:03:22.709 --> 00:03:28.599
Reading is not a hard activity in and of itself
because you're just kind of looking and understanding

00:03:28.599 --> 00:03:29.599
paper.

00:03:29.599 --> 00:03:32.840
But in this day and age with so many distractions,
especially because of the internet - it definitely

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:36.790
is a lot more difficult to eliminate those
distractions and just focus on doing something

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:38.330
a little slower-paced for a while.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:42.250
And while I'm definitely not a book worm right
now, these tips definitely helped me get to

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:46.890
a point where I'm regularly reading good books
and making myself smarter and I feel a lot

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.760
better because of it.

